'''Laze''' '''Loneozner''', also known as "'''Fixer'''", was a [[Gender|male]] [[human]] who lived on the [[Outer Rim Territories|Outer Rim]] [[desert]] [[planet]] [[Tatooine]] during the [[Imperial Era|Age of the Empire]]. He was a childhood friend of [[Luke Skywalker]] and the boyfriend of [[Camie Marstrap]]. Fixer constantly felt out-performed by Skywalker and their friend [[Biggs Darklighter]], and would often put them down using nicknames.<ref name="Card Trader" /> The circle of friends also included [[Deak]] and [[Windy]].<ref name="hopeillustrated">''[[A New Hope: The Princess, the Scoundrel, and the Farm Boy]]''</ref> Loneozner ran [[Tosche Station]], but spent most of his [[time]] talking and tinkering with Skywalker, Darklighter, and Marstrap.<ref name="Complete Locations">[[Star Wars: Complete Locations (2016)|''Star Wars: Complete Locations'']]</ref>

==Biography==
===Early life===
Laze Loneozner [[Homeworld|hailed]] from [[Tatooine]], a [[Star|sun]]-scorched [[desert]] [[planet]] located in the [[Outer Rim Territories]] of [[the galaxy]]. He was a childhood friend of [[Luke Skywalker]] and the boyfriend of [[Camie Marstrap]]. Fixer constantly felt out-performed by Skywalker and their friend [[Biggs Darklighter]], and would often put them down using nicknames.<ref name="Card Trader" />

===A mysterious stranger===
{{Quote|It's not right.''"<br />"''Did you say something?''"<br />"''I said it's not right.|Laze standing up to a Nikto biker|<ref name="Tribes of Tatooine">{{BOBF|Chapter 2: The Tribes of Tatooine}}</ref>}}
[[File:CamieLazeDateNight-BoBFCh2.png|thumb|left|300px|Loneozner and Marstrap witness Boba Fett taking out the Nikto bikers.]]
Sometime after Skywalker's [[Rescue of Han Solo|rescue]] of [[Han Solo]], Loneozner and Marstrap encountered several [[Nikto]] bikers at [[Tosche Station]]. They had several of their things and drinks taken from them. Loneozner verbally protested their actions, something Marstrap attempted to dissuade him from doing but failed to do so. The Niktos then began to rough him up. Marstrap attempted to intervene, shouting for them to stop, but she was restrained by one of the Niktos and was forced to watch the Niktos beat Loneozner with a [[shock stick]]. As he and Marstrap continued to struggle, the Niktos suddenly stopped their attack when [[Boba Fett]] entered the room. The Niktos then attacked Fett who proceeded to dispatch the Niktos one by one while Loneozner and Marstrap huddled in a corner and watched.<ref name="Tribes of Tatooine" />

==Behind the scenes==
{{Quote|Fixer was described to me as a grease-monkey guy, who worked on fixing droids and other stuff. A mechanic. He was also very protective of his girlfriend Camie Marstrap, and very dismissive of Luke, who he called 'Wormy.' Despite our character's on-screen relationship, Mark Hamill and I got along well.|Anthony Forrest|<ref name="Let Me See">{{InsiderCite|216|Let Me See Your Identification}}</ref>}}
[[File:LukeFixerCamieBiggs-TSSOCE.png|thumb|right|250px|Loneozner in a deleted scene from A New Hope.]]
In the original production of [[Star Wars: Episode IV A New Hope|''Star Wars'': Episode IV ''A New Hope'']] (then known as simply ''Star Wars'') in [[1976]], there were several minutes of film involving Luke Skywalker spending time at Tosche power station with his friends. Fixer was played in that scene by [[Anthony Forrest]]. Although those scenes were not used in the final film release, they still appeared in the novelization of the film as well as the [[Star Wars (1977) 1|first issue]] of the [[Star Wars (1977)|''Marvel Star Wars'']] comics adaptation of ''A New Hope''.<ref name="MC1">[[Star Wars (1977) 1|''Star Wars'' (1977) 1]]</ref> They were also retained in the [[1981]] [[Star Wars (radio)|''Star Wars Radio Drama'']] broadcast by [[National Public Radio]]. In this dramatization, Fixer was voiced by [[Adam Arkin]].<ref name="SWR">[[Star Wars (radio)|''Star Wars'' radio drama]]</ref>

Fixer made a few more appearances in various stories and sourcebooks. These sources are part of [[Star Wars Legends|''Star Wars'' Legends]], previously known as the Expanded Universe, and are therefore not official [[canon]].<ref name="EUNewPage">{{SW|url=news/the-legendary-star-wars-expanded-universe-turns-a-new-page|text=The Legendary Star Wars Expanded Universe Turns a New Page}}</ref> However, Fixer and his backstory were partially canonized by [[Topps]]'s app [[Star Wars: Card Trader|''Star Wars'': Card Trader]], which was released in [[2015]].<ref name="Card Trader" />

In "[[Chapter 2: The Tribes of Tatooine]]," the second chapter of the series [[Star Wars: The Book of Boba Fett|''The Book of Boba Fett'']], he was portrayed by [[Skyler Bible]].<ref name="Tribes of Tatooine" />

